    <content:encoded>We both read a lot about flying. Colin regularly reads a few flying blogs and the Aviation News. We both read IFR Training, Aviation Safety, the NTSB Reporter, and a couple other weekly and monthly periodicals. Adam &lt;em&gt;always&lt;/em&gt; read a lot of books about flying, but since starting flight training he has devoured a shelf full. We've been a little slow about reviewing them. Here is a list of the books reviewed in our blog, followed by a list of other books we have read, but have yet to review.

&lt;strong&gt;Reviewed:&lt;/strong&gt;

&lt;a href="http://www.flyingsummers.com/2006/01/01/the-best-flying-books/"&gt;The Proficient Pilot&lt;/a&gt;

&lt;a href="http://www.flyingsummers.com/2005/12/27/real-flying-tips-101-things-to-do/"&gt;Real Flying Tips - 101 Things to Do&lt;/a&gt;

&lt;a href="http://www.flyingsummers.com/2005/11/10/book-free-flight/"&gt;Free Flight&lt;/a&gt;

&lt;a href="http://www.flyingsummers.com/2005/10/24/untitled-post-9/"&gt;Flight of Passage&lt;/a&gt;

&lt;a href="http://www.flyingsummers.com/2005/10/24/untitled-post-7/"&gt;Solo – My Adventures in the Air&lt;/a&gt;

&lt;strong&gt;Read:&lt;/strong&gt;

Lindbergh, by Scott Berg

Inside the Sky

Stick and Rudder

Fate is the Hunter</content:encoded>
